        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add Antigravity pace",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Add Antigravity usage pace support for explicit session and weekly quota-summary windows.\n- Show expected 5-hour pace details for legacy Antigravity model-family rows without mutating their stored window metadata.\n- Preserve the existing compact-icon contract: legacy model-family snapshots remain unknown rather than being relabeled as session/weekly lanes.\n- Add focused coverage for quota-summary rows, legacy rows, lane assignment, and pace boundaries.\n\n## Why\n\nAntigravity quota-summary data provides explicit session and weekly lanes. Older/local snapshots may instead contain model-family quota rows; those rows benefit from pace context in the menu, but they are not equivalent to the compact icon's session and weekly lanes.\n\nThe repaired implementation keeps those two presentation contracts separate: menu rows gain pace details, while the compact icon only uses explicit quota-summary lanes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `swift test --filter Antigravity` — 221 tests passed\n- `swift test --filter UsagePaceTextTests` — 23 tests passed\n- `make check` — passed with the repository Xcode toolchain\n- `make test` — all 48 shards passed\n- Autoreview — no accepted or actionable findings\n- Exact packaged app — Developer ID signature verified; process stayed alive; live menu opened and reopened\n- Source-blind Antigravity row proof — blocked because the existing local configuration had no live Antigravity quota data\n\n## Screenshot\n\nbefore\n<img width=\"311\" height=\"255\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-05 at 16 03 32\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ce5829a0-9720-4484-bd9c-910e6f4f33ab\" />\n\nafter\n<img width=\"309\" height=\"285\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-05 at 4 03 46 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f7aca50f-163f-45cf-a4fa-8a642478e49a\" />\n",
